{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["Some say <b>surar</b> is from the root of sirim, as in 'Behold, I will hedge your way with sirim' (Hosea 2:8). But it seems right to me that it is a past-tense verb from the root of kapparah surarah (Hosea 4:15)."], :book :lamentations, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {0 "The Hosea 4:15 citation refers to the word סוררה; Ibn Ezra likely derives the root from סור in that verse, understanding 'turn aside/away.'"}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Lamentations -- Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%9E%D7%92%D7%99%D7%9C%D7%AA_%D7%90%D7%99%D7%9B%D7%94"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:07:40.550847593Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}